# Mode Study: A Ionian (major) (repertoire plan: st-mode-ionian). An original 16-bar melody over
# a two-chord vamp: Amaj7 (x02120) for two bars, then D (xx0232) for two. The Amaj7 holds G#, the
# colour of Ionian; the D chord has D natural (not D#), which keeps the sound from turning Lydian.
# The melody lands on G# on beat 3 of bars 1, 5, 9 and 13, held, over Amaj7, and uses it as a
# leading note into A at the end of bars 8 and 15. The last bars change faster (D in bar 15,
# Amaj7 in bar 16) so the tune can come home to A.
# Fourth position, one finger per fret: finger 1 on fret 4 (G# on string 1), finger 4 on fret 7.
title: Mode Study: A Ionian (major)
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the Ionian mode
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
